WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.015
Apollo Q Labs. Level one, module two: moneyness and value.

2
00:00:06.315 --> 00:00:12.993
Traders describe an option, a contract on one hundred shares, as in the money, at the money, or out of the money.

3
00:00:12.993 --> 00:00:20.696
In the money, or I T M, means the option has value if exercised, that is, used to buy or sell the shares, right now.

4
00:00:20.696 --> 00:00:31.044
For calls, the right to buy, that means the stock is above the strike, the price the option lets you buy or sell at. For puts, the right to sell, the stock is below the strike.

5
00:00:31.044 --> 00:00:35.973
At the money, or A T M, means the strike is about equal to the stock price.

6
00:00:35.973 --> 00:00:40.540
Out of the money, or O T M, has no value if exercised right now.

7
00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:48.093
It is all time value, the part of the price paid for the chance of a bigger move, and it expires worthless if it stays that way.

8
00:00:48.393 --> 00:00:55.819
Now, what is inside a premium, the price of an option? Premium equals intrinsic value, plus time value.

9
00:00:55.819 --> 00:01:00.663
Intrinsic value is what the option is worth if exercised right now.

10
00:01:00.663 --> 00:01:10.264
Time value, also called extrinsic value, is what traders pay for the chance of a bigger move before expiration, the option’s last day.

11
00:01:10.564 --> 00:01:21.531
Here is an example. The stock is at one hundred and eight dollars, and the one oh five call, the call with a one hundred and five dollar strike, is priced at four dollars and fifty cents.

12
00:01:21.531 --> 00:01:30.087
The stock is above the strike, so the call is in the money. Intrinsic value is one hundred and eight minus one oh five, which is three dollars.

13
00:01:30.087 --> 00:01:34.653
Time value is four fifty minus three dollars, which is one dollar fifty.

14
00:01:34.953 --> 00:01:38.389
Time value shrinks toward zero at expiration.

15
00:01:38.389 --> 00:01:43.340
This shrinking is called time decay, the loss of value as time passes.

16
00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:52.388
Recap: in the money has value if exercised now, out of the money is all time value, and premium is intrinsic value plus time value.

17
00:01:52.388 --> 00:01:55.995
